"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-60","type":"paragraph","en":".border-60"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-61","type":"paragraph","en":"border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--bs-bc) 60%, transparent);"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-62","type":"paragraph","en":".border-70"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-63","type":"paragraph","en":"border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--bs-bc) 70%, transparent);"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-64","type":"paragraph","en":".border-80"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-65","type":"paragraph","en":"border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--bs-bc) 80%, transparent);"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-66","type":"paragraph","en":".border-90"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-67","type":"paragraph","en":"border-color: color-mix(in oklch, var(--bs-bc) 90%, transparent);"}]}]},{"head":false,"cells":[{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-68","type":"paragraph","en":".border-100"}]},{"type":"td","body":[{"id":"content--paragraph-69","type":"paragraph","en":"border-color: var(--bs-bc);"}]}]}]},{"id":"colors","type":"heading","en":"Colors","level":2},{"id":"colors--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Change the <code>border-color</code> using utilities built on our theme colors using <code>.border-{color}</code> and <code>.border-subtle-{color}</code>. All these border color utilities set the <code>border-color</code> property to a local CSS variable, <code>--bs-bc</code>, which has the value of the theme color. The root color tokens color values also use <code>light-dark()</code> to ensure sufficient contrast in both light and dark color modes."},{"id":"colors--paragraph-2","type":"paragraph","en":"For example, <code>.border-primary</code> sets the <code>--bs-bc</code> variable to <code>var(--bs-primary-border)</code>:"},{"id":"colors--code-1","type":"code","value":".border-primary {\n  --bs-bc: var(--bs-primary-border);\n  border-color: var(--bs-bc);\n}","language":""},{"id":"colors--paragraph-3","type":"paragraph","en":"This approach allows us to also easily support translucency with our <code>.border-{opacity}</code> utilities as we can use <code>color-mix()</code> with the CSS variable to generate the appropriate color. See the <a href=\"#opacity\">opacity section</a> for more details."},{"id":"colors--note-1","type":"note","tone":"info","body":[{"id":"colors--note-text-1","type":"note-text","en":"The <code>--bs-bc</code> variable is registered with <code>@property</code> as non-inheriting (<code>inherits: false</code>), so border color utilities are scoped to the element they’re applied to and never cascade into nested elements or components. This is why <code>--bs-bc</code> is deliberately separate from the inheriting <code>--bs-border-color</code> design token that components resolve their default borders from."}]},{"id":"colors--example-1","type":"demo","key":"8495669d229571f7bea0","height":300},{"id":"colors--code-2","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary\">primary</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-primary\">primary subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-accent\">accent</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-accent\">accent subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-success\">success</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-success\">success subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-danger\">danger</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-danger\">danger subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-warning\">warning</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-warning\">warning subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-info\">info</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-info\">info subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-inverse\">inverse</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-inverse\">inverse subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-secondary\">secondary</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-secondary\">secondary subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-bg\">bg</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-body\">body</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-muted\">muted</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle\">subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-emphasized\">emphasized</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-black\">black</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-white\">white</div>","language":""},{"id":"colors--paragraph-4","type":"paragraph","en":"Or modify the default <code>border-color</code> of a component:"},{"id":"colors--example-2","type":"demo","key":"3c0aba0fee2ea5939afd","height":201,"anchors":["exampleFormControlInput1"]},{"id":"colors--code-3","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"mb-4\">\n  <label for=\"exampleFormControlInput1\" class=\"form-label\">Email address</label>\n  <input type=\"email\" class=\"form-control border-success\" id=\"exampleFormControlInput1\" placeholder=\"name@example.com\">\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"h4 pb-2 mb-4 fg-danger border-bottom border-danger\">\n  Dangerous heading\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"p-3 bg-info bg-10 border border-info border-start-0 rounded-end\">\n  Changing border color and width\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"nested-elements","type":"heading","en":"Nested elements","level":2},{"id":"nested-elements--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Because border color utilities set the non-inheriting <code>--bs-bc</code> variable, parent border colors don’t affect the borders of nested elements. Below, the parent uses <code>.border-danger</code> while the nested <code>.border</code> keeps the default border color."},{"id":"nested-elements--example-1","type":"demo","key":"89f627a3e51f70a72cc1","height":147},{"id":"nested-elements--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"p-3 border border-danger rounded-5\">\n  Parent with .border-danger\n  <div class=\"border p-3 mt-3\">\n    Nested .border keeps the default color\n  </div>\n</div>","language":""},{"id":"opacity","type":"heading","en":"Opacity","level":2},{"id":"opacity--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Change the opacity of a border color by using any of the <code>.border-&lt;percentage&gt;</code> utilities which use <code>color-mix()</code> to mix the border color with <code>transparent</code> thanks to the CSS variable approach mentioned above. Because <code>--bs-bc</code> is scoped to the element, pair these opacity utilities with a <code>.border-{color}</code> utility on the same element—they no longer inherit a border color from an ancestor."},{"id":"opacity--example-1","type":"demo","key":"8b2b1723ab9f8f87c911","height":300},{"id":"opacity--code-1","type":"code","value":"<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary p-2 mb-2\">Default border</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-90 p-2 mb-2\">90% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-80 p-2 mb-2\">80% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-70 p-2 mb-2\">70% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-60 p-2 mb-2\">60% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-50 p-2 mb-2\">50% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-40 p-2 mb-2\">40% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-30 p-2 mb-2\">30% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-20 p-2 mb-2\">20% opacity</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary border-10 p-2\">10% opacity</div>","language":""},{"id":"css","type":"heading","en":"CSS","level":2},{"id":"variables","type":"heading","en":"Variables","level":3},{"id":"variables--code-1","type":"code","value":"--border-width: #{$border-width},\n--border-width-keyline: .5px,\n--border-style: #{$border-style},\n--border-color: light-dark(var(--gray-200), var(--gray-700)),\n--border-color-translucent: color-mix(in oklch, var(--fg-body) 15%, transparent),","language":""},{"id":"sass-variables","type":"heading","en":"Sass variables","level":3},{"id":"sass-variables--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Variables for setting <code>border-color</code> in <code>.border-*-subtle</code> utilities in light and dark mode:"},{"id":"sass-utilities-api","type":"heading","en":"Sass utilities API","level":3},{"id":"sass-utilities-api--paragraph-1","type":"paragraph","en":"Border color utilities are declared in our utilities API in <code>scss/_utilities.scss</code>. <a href=\"https://getbootstrap.com/docs/6.0/utilities/api#using-the-api\">Learn how to use the utilities API.</a>"},{"id":"sass-utilities-api--code-1","type":"code","value":"\"border-color\": (\n  property: (\n    \"--bc\": null,\n    \"border-color\": var(--bc)\n  ),\n  class: border,\n  values: map.merge(theme-color-refs(\"bg\"), theme-token-refs($theme-borders, \"border\")),\n),\n\"border-color-subtle\": (\n  property: (\n    \"--bc\": null,\n    \"border-color\": var(--bc)\n  ),\n  class: border-subtle,\n  values: theme-color-refs(\"border\"),\n),\n\"border-width\": (\n  property: border-width,\n  class: border,\n  values: map.merge($border-widths, (keyline: var(--border-width-keyline)))\n),\n\"border-opacity\": (\n  class: border,\n  property: border-color,\n  values: theme-opacity-values(--bc)\n),","language":""}],"demos":[{"key":"8495669d229571f7bea0","html":"<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary\">primary</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-primary\">primary subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-accent\">accent</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-accent\">accent subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-success\">success</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-success\">success subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-danger\">danger</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-danger\">danger subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-warning\">warning</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-warning\">warning subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-info\">info</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-info\">info subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-inverse\">inverse</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-inverse\">inverse subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-secondary\">secondary</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle-secondary\">secondary subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-bg\">bg</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-body\">body</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-muted\">muted</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-subtle\">subtle</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-emphasized\">emphasized</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-black\">black</div>\n<div class=\"border border-5 border-white\">white</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example d-flex flex-column gap-2 bd-example-border-color-utils"},"sprite":""},{"key":"3c0aba0fee2ea5939afd","html":"<div class=\"mb-4\">\n  <label for=\"exampleFormControlInput1\" class=\"form-label\">Email address</label>\n  <input type=\"email\" class=\"form-control border-success\" id=\"exampleFormControlInput1\" placeholder=\"name@example.com\">\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"h4 pb-2 mb-4 fg-danger border-bottom border-danger\">\n  Dangerous heading\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"p-3 bg-info bg-10 border border-info border-start-0 rounded-end\">\n  Changing border color and width\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"89f627a3e51f70a72cc1","html":"<div class=\"p-3 border border-danger rounded-5\">\n  Parent with .border-danger\n  <div class=\"border p-3 mt-3\">\n    Nested .border keeps the default color\n  </div>\n</div>","attrs":{"class":"bd-example"},"sprite":""},{"key":"8b2b1723ab9f8f87c911","html":"<div class=\"border border-5 border-primary p-2